    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605-a1">

                <pb facs="0652" n="602" xml:id="pg602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosnre in No. 108.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Moret.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-15"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Permit me to thank you for your note
                    of the 10th instant, in which you inform me that the Cuban repertory has
                    arrived; that it is being compared (se esta confrontando); and that at the
                    earliest possible moment it will be sent to Cuba so that it may be immediately
                    carried out. The contents of your note I cabled to Washington, and I at once
                    received in reply a cablegram in which the Secretary of State says that he can
                    not understand with what document the repertory is being compared, as it has
                    already been compared by the Spanish legation in Washington with the original in
                    that capital. I am instructed to earnestly request its publication in Cuba at
                    the earliest possible moment, as errors are continually arising there from the
                    use of the unauthorized version. Will you be so good as to inform me, at your
                    earliest convenience, how soon the publication of the authorized version will be
                    made in Cuba so that I may inform my Government by cable?</p>
                <p>I seize, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
